## Why This Is Asked

Introduces a new angle: tenant-aware, region-spanning telemetry with cost-aware data reduction via adaptive sampling and policy routing, a realistic high-load scenario.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant-aware adaptive sampling policy stored in DynamoDB
- Exactly-once processing across regions with idempotent writes
- Flow control to S3/Glue based on routing rules and SLAs
- OpenTelemetry tracing across Lambda/Fargate
- Cost governance and testing under churn

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: compute per-tenant sampling rate from traffic, SLA, and budget
function samplingRate(tenantId, metrics) {
  const {throughput, budget} = metrics[tenantId] || {throughput: 0, budget: 1};
  const target = Math.max(0.01, Math.min(1, budget / Math.max(throughput, 1)));
  return target;
}
```

